							<span class="title"><strong><font face="Arial" size="2">Application Process Explained</font></strong></span> <hr size="1" /> Applying to Inverse Logic is a process requiring several steps. Please read the overview and all <br /><br /><!--EZCODE FONT START--><span style="FONT-SIZE: medium; COLOR: orange"><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong><font color="#deb887">The Application Process:</font></strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--></span><!--EZCODE FONT END--><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>1.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> Make sure you meet the <!--EZCODE LINK START--><a href="custom.aspx?pid=1178" target="top">general requirements</a><!--EZCODE LINK END-->.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>2.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> Fill out the <!--EZCODE LINK START--><a href="custom.aspx?pid=1177" target="top">application form</a><!--EZCODE LINK END--> and send it in. Make sure you put in your Magelo info or this might slow down the process.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>3.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> After we receive your application you will get an email back letting you know if it has been put up for screening as well as info about our application channel.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>4.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> Most applications spend a day or two in screening after which it is either rejected or passed on to the members for review. You will recieve another email at this time letting you know how it is going.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>5.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> If your application was accepted you will have two weeks to secure a sponsor if you do not already have one. If you do not get one after the end of the two weeks you can reapply again after a month.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>6.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> When you have secured a sponsor you will get a guild tag and your probabtion period will begin. You should now <!--EZCODE LINK START--><a href="http://p202.ezboard.com/finverselogicfrm14" target="top">post</a><!--EZCODE LINK END--> for access to the messageboard forums.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>7.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> The probation period is 3 weeks. After the first two weeks a one week vote will be put up for the members to determine if you will be a full member.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>8.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> You need 60% yes votes to become a full member. If you do not get that and you dont have 2 no votes your probation period will be extended with another 3 weeks.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>9.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> If you after your second probation still do not have enough yes votes to make it as full member you can reapply again after a month.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE FONT START--><span style="FONT-SIZE: medium; COLOR: orange"><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong><font color="#deb887">Alittle extra info for probies and applicants:</font></strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--></span><!--EZCODE FONT END--><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Raid Invites</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- Your friend who invites you to the raid will go over any rules that might apply. You are not allowed to attend raids unless someone on the raid invites you and the person that invites you clear it with an officer.<br /><br />- Some raids may have level restrictions, or limited numbers allowed.<br /><br />- Raid invites do not carry guildtag, unless needed for communications.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Loot, Flags keys and Sneaks:</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- While you are an applicant and a probie with IL you should not be expecting the guild to reward you with loot. There may be times when loot is offered to invites and probies but as a rule all loot will be awarded to full members first.<br /><br />- As a probie you are expected to work on getting your keys and flags you are missing. The guild will help where it can, but we might not always be able to work on just the flag you are missing or the key piece you need. Please understand that it isnt because we dont want to help you, but full member flagging will be a priority.<br /><br />- When we raid in zones you are not flagged for you should not be expecting to get a sneak unless all the full members have been snuck in first or we specifically need someone of your class. <br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Bots and Alts:</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- While on probation you are expected to play your main char at all times when raiding/grouping with the guild. We are interested in getting to know you as a person yes, but we are also interested in seeing how well you play your class.<br /><br />- If you like botting you will be limited to only bringing one bot to any raid. If you have more than one you are welcome to ask an officer which of them would be most useful, otherwise please bring your primary bot to the raids.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Applicants</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- If you are currently tagged with a guild, remove the tag before sending in the application.<br /><br />- As applicant, you should not have any open applications with other guilds. If such are found, your application with Inverse Logic will be closed.<br /><br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Sponsorship</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- Each full member of Inverse Logic can be a sponsor for applicants. The sponsorship must be confirmed through posting on the application in question, or contacting an officer.<br /><br />- Each person who has posted sponsorship for someone is expected to assist that player in getting to know the guild, and introducing them to others. <br /><br />Details about the 3 week probationary period<br />- Only your main character will carry guildtag during this period, so please choose the right character to apply with. It is important that you group and raid with IL with the character with which you applied, so we can attach a name with a face.<br /><br />- During your 3 week trial, please try to meet people in the guild and talk to them. You should try to meet people both in raids and in exp groups, as each situation will show different sides of you.<br /><br />- You can also get to know people through reading and posting on our messageboard forums.<br /><br />- If something unforeseen prevents you from playing with us for a noticeable portion of the trial period, let us know through a post so people can take that into account when voting. If you will be unable to play for a long period, consider terminating the application and reapplying later.<br /><br />- The 3 week trial period is a critical time used to get to know other members and determine if this is the right guild for you. Do not expect nor demand any large guild effort or support towards personal gains such as quests or gear acquisition. The trial period is best spent finding your place within the guild, not what you can obtain from it. Gain the support and loyalty of your fellow guildmates upon becoming a full member, and you will more likely receive the help you need. <br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Additional 3 week trial</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br />- Don't view this as punishment for not being online, consider it instead as an extra chance granted for those who have real life commitments or other reasons which make three weeks too short a time to get to know us.<br /><br />- Try hard during this second trial period to meet different persons than the ones you met in the first trial period, as the most likely reason for the insufficient votes is that you did not get to know enough people.<br /><br />- Ask your sponsor to help, and introduce you to playing with others.<br />
							
